s.save(B/'summary.json',{'batch_id':selection['batch_id'],'status':'all_twenty_scoped_steps_reviewed','counts':counts,'integration':integration,'preserved_prior_files':len(preserved),'remaining_unrun_prompts':sum(not n.get('latest_run') for n in json.loads((s.ROOT/'dag/operads/index.json').read_bytes())['nodes']),'scope':'Twenty local staged scoped results/obstructions; no blanket original-target, physical, full-operad-coherence or authority promotion.'})
readme='# PFP prompts 72 through 91\n\nTwenty previously unrun prompts executed locally through P0/P1/P2/P4/P5, with P3 for actual failed native gates. Every stage retains operad deltas, exact input/source bindings and actual checker/native results. Original failed attempts and setup refusals remain preserved. A transient canonical collection write also failed during review; custody/review_write_failure.json retains that failure and tools/resume_review.py checks existing review bytes before resuming only the unfinished nodes. One P2 checkpoint lost output recording to disk exhaustion: its Rust exit status is explicitly unknown, and a fresh named retry supplies the accepted result. The actual work-unit hypotheses are added to reviewed ambient slots separately from the historical source assumption list, so an empty source list is not promoted into an assumption-free result. No external provider was dispatched; active chat cost is unmeasured. One local Codex researcher performed the scope review.\n\n'+json.dumps(counts,sort_keys=True)+'\n\n'+json.dumps(integration,sort_keys=True)+'\n\nThe selected base includes upstream PR83. Its additive Majorana facade re-exports made one file-only source-lead pin stale; the initial P0 preparation refused it. Both source versions and the narrow public-export diff are retained in custody/, along with the original collection, initial request and failed resume. The successful successor uses a distinct snapshot path. No implementation or physical claim is promoted by that metadata repair.\n\nThe mathematical review separates declared registry/antecedent fields from real validation, a finite queue from a threshold theorem, repetition-code guarantees from arbitrary stabilizer/homology bounds, Q8 from quantum gravity, finite proxy separation from physical-import independence, and not-exponent-two from topological connectedness. The finite-map bundle receives a scoped Kellner-polynomial stage only; its other rows and physical integral/ansatz imports remain explicit. Actual contextual/code error tables, full Choi matrices, tomography effects and gamma/parity arrays replace route-index or provider-PASS proxies. The Majorana gate caught a real Rust commutator/anticommutator sign error; its failed checkpoint and before/after source versions remain in source_repair/. P3 corrects the sign without altering the Python numerical certificate. Every run is freshly replayed on the repaired final Rust source.\n\nNative arrays and literal finite/rational Lean statements have separate scopes. Full refined-carrier operad identity/substitution/symmetry/coherence, physical transport and original target closure remain open where stated. Cached pinned Mathlib is imported; no full Mathlib/transitive-dependency/whole-repository or hosted-CI claim is made. Counts are unique tests/theorems, not sums of repeated gates. Historical filename-custody paper pins remain explicit and unchanged. Prior results/prompts and unrelated operad collections are checked against their base Git blobs in review/preservation.json.\n\n| Prompt | Supported step | Remaining obligation |\n|---|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join(table)+'\n\nRead-only replay:\n\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 -O verify_batch.py\n    py -3.9 -X utf8 test_custody_guards.py -v\n\nGitHub delivery state is independently verified after publication. AuthorityEffect: None.\n'
(B/'README.md').write_bytes(readme.encode());paths.add(s.ROOT/'dag/operads/index.json');paths.update(p for p in B.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and '__pycache__' not in p.parts)
s.save(B/'manifest.json',{'scope':'All owned batch/run/review artifacts and exact construction/build/collection source bytes, excluding this manifest itself. Prior historical files have a separate Git-blob preservation receipt.','files':[s.pin(p) for p in sorted(paths)]})
